  BEGINNER
================================================================

What is Docker?
---------------
Docker lets you package applications into containers —
lightweight, portable environments that run the same way
everywhere, regardless of the underlying system.


Installation Check
------------------
  docker --version
  docker info


Basic Concepts
--------------
  Image       -> Blueprint/template for creating a container
  Container   -> A running instance of an image
  Dockerfile  -> Script to build a custom image
  Registry    -> Storage for images (e.g. Docker Hub)


First Commands
--------------
  # Pull an image from Docker Hub
  docker pull ubuntu

  # Run a container
  docker run ubuntu

  # Run interactively (with terminal)
  docker run -it ubuntu bash

  # List running containers
  docker ps

  # List ALL containers (including stopped)
  docker ps -a

  # List downloaded images
  docker images

  # Stop a container
  docker stop <container_id>

  # Remove a container
  docker rm <container_id>

  # Remove an image
  docker rmi ubuntu


